# Commit each completed change

This repository has a standing request to commit agent work. When you finish a change the user asked for, commit it before you end the turn. Each commit is one rollback unit: a bad change is undone with `git revert <sha>`.

## When to commit

- Commit once the change is complete. Leave a half-finished or still-broken edit uncommitted.
- One logical change per commit. Unrelated requests in the same thread get separate commits.
- Stage only files you changed for that request. Leave pre-existing dirty and untracked files out.
- Skip the commit when there is nothing new to commit, the user said not to commit, or the diff contains secrets (`.env`, credentials, keys). Warn instead of committing secrets.

## How to commit

No git config changes, no `--no-verify`, no force push, no `git push` unless the user asks, and no amend unless the amend rules are already met.

In parallel, run `git status`, `git diff` (staged and unstaged), and `git log -8 --oneline`. Then stage the files for this change and commit. The subject is one imperative line, specific enough to recognize later, in the same short style as recent history.

```bash
git commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
fix hold timer resetting when continuous is checked

EOF
)"
```

Run `git status` after the commit. In your reply, include the short hash and subject so the user can revert that commit.
